wback,Tradition - Oathbound Casting: Oath of Loyalty (1 drawback point)	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Casting Drawback,Tradition - Oathbound Casting: Oath of Offerings (7 drawback points)	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Casting Drawback,Tradition - Oathbound Casting: Oath of Poverty (10 drawback points)	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Casting Drawback,Tradition - Oathbound Casting: Oath of Ritual (1 drawback point)	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Casting Drawback,Tradition - Oathbound Casting: Oath of Secrecy (1 drawback point)	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Casting Drawback,Tradition - Oathbound Casting: Oath of Silence (2 drawback points)	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Casting Drawback,Tradition - Oathbound Casting: Oath of Wardenship (3 drawback points)	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Casting Drawback,Tradition - Oathbound Casting: Oath of the Cryptkeeper (1 drawback point)	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Custom Casting Boon|1	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_TRADITION_DRAWBACKS|1	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Oath Adjudication,Reviewed - Oath of Devotion	DESC:Grants 1 drawback point (counts as 1 drawbacks and costs none). Source: Baron's Otherworldly Citadel Oath: Your powerful feelings for a specific person fuel your outlook and passion. Choose a person important to you at GM discretion. You may not speak badly of them, break a promise to them, snub their gestures of friendship, turn down their requests, or place your dedication to another person [besides yourself] above your dedication to the person. If you have to choose between the person’s commands and a violation against social or moral law or a specific code of conduct, the GM is responsible for deciding if you have kept to the spirit of the Oath. Defiance Penalty: In crossing the subject of your devotion, you are left purposeless and adrift. You take a penalty on all skill checks equal to half your character level. Atonement: To atone, you must confess your discretions to your chosen person and receive their forgiveness. If both apology and forgiveness are sincere, you regain your abilities after 24 hours. Breaking, forsaking, or lacking this oath suspends spellcasting until atonement or a new 8-hour oath.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/oaths#toc14
