wback,Tradition - Oathbound Casting: Oath of Loyalty (1 drawback point)	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Casting Drawback,Tradition - Oathbound Casting: Oath of Offerings (7 drawback points)	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Casting Drawback,Tradition - Oathbound Casting: Oath of Poverty (10 drawback points)	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Casting Drawback,Tradition - Oathbound Casting: Oath of Ritual (1 drawback point)	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Casting Drawback,Tradition - Oathbound Casting: Oath of Secrecy (1 drawback point)	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Casting Drawback,Tradition - Oathbound Casting: Oath of Silence (2 drawback points)	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Casting Drawback,Tradition - Oathbound Casting: Oath of Wardenship (3 drawback points)	!PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Custom Casting Drawback,Tradition - Oathbound Casting: Oath of the Cryptkeeper (1 drawback point)	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Custom Casting Boon|3	BONUS:VAR|SPHERES_TRADITION_DRAWBACKS|3	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=Spheres Oath Adjudication,Reviewed - Oath of Expedience	DESC:Grants 3 drawback points (counts as 3 drawbacks and costs none). Source: Baron's Otherworldly Citadel Oath: In times of trouble, you move with continued forward action. In combat, you cannot willingly perform full-round actions or actions that take 1 round or more, nor can you willingly take 10 or 20 on rolls. Defiance Penalty: The opportunities you stand to lose unnerve you. You take a penalty on Fortitude and Will saving throws equal to half your character level [minimum -2]. Atonement: You must make up for what you perceive as lost time and potential, spending three nights without sleeping [this causes you to become fatigued and exhausted as normal]. Breaking, forsaking, or lacking this oath suspends spellcasting until atonement or a new 8-hour oath.	SOURCEPAGE:https://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/oaths#toc15
